                        "sense_id": "57302587-ed64-3876-a24d-443431700943",
                        "entry_id": "ecf080c0-1f07-3358-9a9a-133ce092cfcd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A few silk threads or horsehairs, or a strip of linen etc., introduced beneath the skin by a knife or needle, so as to induce suppuration; also, the issue so formed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6787c379-edbd-4745-bf01-7654bb9bdd03",
                                "sense_id": "57302587-ed64-3876-a24d-443431700943",
                                "text": "If the predisposition to the disease has arisen from a plethoric state of the system, or from a turgescence in the vessels of the head, this is to be obviated by bleeding, both generally and topically, but more particularly the latter; an abstemious diet and proper exercise; and by a seton in the neck."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e034a83-fe28-4e95-8c2a-f84e70f9d55f",
                                "sense_id": "57302587-ed64-3876-a24d-443431700943",
                                "text": "The animal was lean and tall, and had a moth-eaten mane, rough hoofs and loose shoes; a seton bobbed up and down on its breast."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
